    {"title":"a - a +0 robe (worn).","body":"<lightgrey>\n\nA large, loose-fitting, wide-sleeved outer garment made of light cloth. It offers little protection against physical harm, but does not hinder evasion or spellcasting. \n\nBase armour rating: 2       Encumbrance rating: 0\n\nIt can be maximally enchanted to +2.\n\nIf you take off this armour:\nYour AC would decrease by 2.0 (2.0 -> 0.0).\nYour EV would remain unchanged.\n\n\nStash search prefixes: {inventory} {body armour} {body armor}\nMenu/colouring prefixes: identified equipped armour\n_________________\n\n<darkgrey>“CLEOPATRA: Give me my robe, put on my crown; I have\n Immortal longings in me”\n    -William Shakespeare, _Anthony & Cleopatra_, V, ii. ca. 1605.\n<lightgrey>SPELLSET_PLACEHOLDER","spellset":[],"actions":"(t)ake off, (d)rop, (=)adjust, or (i)nscribe.","tiles":[{"t":5209,"tex":4},{"t":3883,"tex":4}],"msg":"ui-push","type":"describe-item","ui-centred":false,"generation_id":9},
